{#- Credential strip. Added August 27, 2026, rebuilt the same day.

    ONE COMPACT ROW OF MARKS. Names only — `item.note` is deliberately never
    rendered here. The first version printed the notes too, and under a photo
    hero it became a ~450px wall of explanatory copy in a ragged 3+2 grid where
    badged rows were indented and text-only rows were not, so nothing aligned.
    A trust strip is glanced at; the explanation belongs on the About page,
    which is linked from the closing line and where someone has chosen to read.

    Content lives in _data/credentials.json, never here.

    `variant` (optional, set by the including page):
      "full"    — default. Label, marks, the Coach Match line, About link.
      "compact" — marks only, for pages that already link to the About page.  -#}
{%- set cr = credentials[lang] -%}
{%- set variant = trustBarVariant or "full" -%}
<section class="trust-bar{% if variant == "compact" %} trust-bar-compact{% endif %}">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="label">{{ cr.barLabel }}</span>
    <ul class="trust-marks">
      {%- for item in cr.items %}
      <li class="trust-mark{% if item.badge %} has-badge{% endif %}">
        {%- if item.badge %}
        {#- width/height prevent reflow while loading. `loading="lazy"` is
            deliberately not used: on the homepage this sits under the hero. -#}
        <img class="trust-badge" src="{{ item.badge | v }}" alt="{{ item.badgeAlt }}" width="40" height="40" decoding="async">
        {%- endif %}
        <span class="trust-mark-name">{{ item.short or item.name }}</span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- if variant != "compact" %}
    <p class="trust-line">{{ cr.barLine }} <a href="{{ cr.aboutHref }}">{{ cr.aboutLabel }} &rarr;</a></p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>
